      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "The most similar analogue, m-AMSA, an acridine methanesulfonamide, had CSF concentrations only 1-3% of plasma in rhesus monkeys after IV dosing, directly demonstrating poor BBB penetration for this acridine/sulfonamide chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C17"],
      "claim": "A methanesulfonamide-containing fused heteroaromatic analogue showed a brain-to-plasma ratio of 0.07 in rat, indicating low CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "PK11195, a lipophilic aryl-substituted heteroaryl carboxamide, is reported to have low brain penetration in PET studies, a limitation noted for this structural class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C12"],
      "claim": "A close analogue sharing the chiral N-(1-phenylpropyl) carboxamide side chain showed excellent brain penetration and no P-gp efflux, providing a countervailing positive signal for the amide side chain.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C19"],
      "claim": "PK11195 extraction from blood to brain was reported as rapid and high (>90%) and unimpeded by the BBB, indicating that some lipophilic heteroaryl carboxamides can achieve meaningful brain delivery.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted fail. The strongest transferable evidence (acridine methanesulfonamide m-AMSA) shows very low CSF/plasma, and additional sulfonamide/fused-heteroaryl negatives support poor CNS access. Positive chiral-amide side-chain and PK11195 extraction data are less structurally transferable and do not overcome the acridine/sulfonamide liabilities.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain or CSF measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "PK11195 records are contradictory, with some reporting high BBB extraction and others reporting low brain penetration.",
    "Acridine dihydropyridine prodrug positives are not directly applicable to the neutral parent query."
  ],
